+def sym_score_grid_fast_for[column: Int]() -> Bool:
+    """SCHEDULING row (lane/apple-fast-yetirank, 2026-10-02): whether the
+    symmetric level's score launch (`compute_optimal_splits_kernel`, the
+    `sym.score` stage of `tree_search`) runs one thread per bin feature
+    instead of CatBoost's grid-strided 64 blocks. `-D
+    MOJOLEARN_YETI_TREE_SEARCH_SCORE_GRID=1`, FAST on Apple only, default
+    off; `sym_argmax_blocks_for` reads it.
+
+    CAUSE. The reference grid is `min(64, ceil(binFeatures / 256))` blocks
+    of `SCORE_BLOCK_SIZE` (128) threads: 8192 threads for Istella's ~56k
+    bin features, each walking 7 bin features x every live leaf (64 at
+    depth 6) x the stat planes through dependent global loads. On the
+    M3 Ultra's 80 cores that is a tenth of one wave, and the stage is
+    latency bound. With one thread per bin feature the same per-thread
+    walk runs once, on `ceil(binFeatures / 128)` blocks (440 for Istella,
+    capped at `SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST_CAP`).
+
+    SAME BITS. A bin feature's score is computed by exactly one thread
+    in the same order (leaves in `part_ids` order, stats in order) on
+    either grid; the noise draw is seeded by the feature id alone. The
+    block argmax and the level resolve (`resolve_and_pack_kernel`,
+    `sym_resolve_split_count_kernel`, both loop over `argmax_blocks`)
+    apply one total order, higher gain then the smaller bin feature, so
+    the winner does not depend on how the bin features are partitioned
+    into blocks. The one corner where a partition could matter is a
+    block every one of whose bin features is skipped or scores `-inf`
+    (a feature weight above 1 on a degenerate denominator): its sentinel
+    `(-FLOAT32_MAX, 0xFFFFFFFF)` outranks a `-inf` gain; the reference
+    grid has the same corner with its own partition. `aft_ab.sh` prints
+    the model hashes, which must agree."""
+    comptime if is_defined["MOJOLEARN_YETI_TREE_SEARCH_SCORE_GRID"]():
+        return column == COLUMN_APPLE and GLOBAL_NUMERIC_MODE == NUMERIC_FAST
+    return False
+
+
+comptime SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST = sym_score_grid_fast_for[TARGET_COLUMN]()
+#: the FAST grid's block cap: the resolve kernels loop over the block
+#: winners sequentially on every thread, so the cap bounds that loop
+comptime SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST_CAP = 1024
+
+
 def sym_argmax_blocks_for(hist_cells_per_leaf: Int) -> Int:
     """The symmetric score launch's grid (and the `out_score`/`out_bin`
     partials it writes): `min(64, ceil(cells / 256))`, at least 1, the
-    reference sizing. The workspace allocation and the level loop both size
-    through here so the partials always fit. (The FAST one-thread-per-bin-
-    feature grid, `-D MOJOLEARN_YETI_TREE_SEARCH_SCORE_GRID`, was
-    DROPPED-noise; lane/apple-fast-yetirank @ c7b35fd7c.)"""
+    reference sizing; under `SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST` one `SCORE_BLOCK_SIZE`
+    block per `SCORE_BLOCK_SIZE` bin features, capped (the docstring
+    above). The workspace allocation and the level loop both size through
+    here so the partials always fit."""
+    comptime if SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST:
+        var fast_blocks = (
+            hist_cells_per_leaf + SCORE_BLOCK_SIZE - 1
+        ) // SCORE_BLOCK_SIZE
+        if fast_blocks > SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST_CAP:
+            fast_blocks = SYM_SCORE_GRID_FAST_CAP
+        if fast_blocks < 1:
+            fast_blocks = 1
+        return fast_blocks
     var argmax_blocks = (hist_cells_per_leaf + 255) // 256
     if argmax_blocks > 64:
         argmax_blocks = 64
